/**

@page page_peano_localisation Localisation of generated data

\tableofcontents

Peano keeps one replicated grid structure per rank and rank-local pools for
generated cell, face, and vertex data. Traversal events map the global tree
entity indices to the pool slots relevant to the current rank and subtree
task.

# Rank-local pools

Each generated data type owns a peano4::grid::StackContainer. Its flat pool
contains slots for locally relevant entities, rank-boundary frozen copies, and
subtree-task interface copies. An event uses
peano4::grid::GridTraversalObserver::NoData for an entity that has no data in
the current rank traversal.

Cells have one owning rank. Faces and vertices can have slots on several ranks
when cells from those ranks touch them. Their generated merge routine combines
the partner copies before the first consuming callback.

# Storage predicates

Generated data types provide static `load()` and `store()` predicates that
receive the entity marker. On a first touch, `load()` decides whether the pool
slot moves into the observer's call block. On a last touch, `store()` decides
whether the call-block value moves back into the persistent pool slot.

Repeated touches within one observer always preserve the call-block value.
Creation and destruction events use their dedicated lifecycle callbacks and do
not load a standing pool value.

Storage predicates are suitable for temporary data and data that exists only
on selected entities. A disabled first touch receives a default object, so an
action set does not observe stale content from a reused call-block position.

# Task-local copies

A parallel traversal redirects a face or vertex that two subtree tasks hold to
the live slot of the current subtree task. Each task completes its first-touch
and last-touch lifecycle on that copy. The post-sweep merge freezes the result,
and the next sweep merges partner copies according to the generated data policy.

A generated container can reject this copy protocol through its subtree-task
replication property. If any container rejects it, the rank traversal remains
serial.

# Markers

Vertex, face, and cell markers report rank locality, hanging state, refinement
state, position, and mesh width for the selected event entity. Action sets use
these marker queries in their storage and compute predicates. They do not infer
locality from a tree identifier or a pool-slot value.

*/
